**Potential Bug:** The cleanup condition on line 51 will never be true. The value stored in `locks.set()` is `currentLock.then(() => nextLock)` (a new Promise), but the comparison checks `=== nextLock`. These are different promise objects, so the lock entries will never be deleted and will accumulate in memory.

Suggestion: Store `nextLock` directly instead of the chained promise, or track a different reference for cleanup.

```suggestion
    const chained = currentLock.then(() => nextLock)
    current.locks.set(filepath, chained)
    await currentLock
    try {
      const result = await fn()
      return result
    } finally {
      release()
      if (current.locks.get(filepath) === chained) {
        current.locks.delete(filepath)
      }
    }
```

